
dist/

# NOT `assets/` wholesale. Two things under it are BUILD INPUTS that must ship: assets/fonts/,
# which the viewer links, and assets/view_local.toml, the one scene a `trunk serve` shows - both
# are named by index.html, so a checkout without them cannot `trunk build` at all. Only the scene
# DATA below is untracked.

# Scene data lives in the R2 bucket, never in the repo. `DATA_BASE` in src/app/persistence.rs
# names the host and every manifest and .pb resolves against it, so nothing here has to ship.
# The files stay on disk as an UNTRACKED cache: docs/_gate.sh renders them locally to compare
# pixels, and a gate that cannot open a scene cannot catch a rendering regression.
# assets/fonts/ is NOT here - those are build inputs the viewer links, not scene data.
# assets/pb/* not assets/pb/: git does not descend into an excluded DIRECTORY, so a negation
# inside one is dead. index.html declares `copy-dir href="assets/pb"`, which means a checkout
# without that directory cannot `trunk build` AT ALL - .gitkeep is what makes a fresh clone build.
assets/pb/*
!assets/pb/.gitkeep
assets/scenes/
assets/pdf/
assets/lion_src/
